# Higurashi Loop refinement

Run in the main conversation and accept one opaque work-item ID with an
optional `--from <project-relative-path>` from `$ARGUMENTS`. The user may
instead paste a requirement in the conversation. Load the project-local
`higurashi-refine` skill as the canonical contract. If it is unavailable, stop
and report an incomplete adapter install.

Do not alter control documents, generated ownership markers, or existing tests to bypass required behavior; report a blocker instead.

1. Run `higurashi inspect <ID> --json`. If it is not `kind: ready`, import only
   an explicitly supplied file or pasted requirement. For a file, run
   `higurashi requirements import <ID> --from <PATH> --json`. For pasted text,
   show the exact text, require confirmation that it is authoritative, and pass
   it verbatim to `higurashi requirements import <ID> --stdin --json`. Never
   paraphrase, infer, search for, replace, or silently select a requirement.
   Stop on conflict. Re-inspect and require `kind: ready`.
2. Invoke `higurashi-loop:higurashi-refine` in `questions` stage with the exact
   inspection result and requirement source. Present its single question batch,
   including every recommended answer, and accept one free-text response.
3. Invoke the same agent in `draft` stage with that response. If it returns a
   follow-up batch, present it and accept one more free-text response. Permit at most one follow-up, then require a complete draft or stop unresolved.
4. Show the complete draft and request explicit confirmation. Do not treat
   silence, an unrelated response, or partial answer acceptance as confirmation.
5. Only after confirmation, invoke the agent in `persist` stage with the exact
   confirmed contract. Require it to re-inspect, create only the returned
   artifact path with `Status: refined`, and return a fresh inspection hash.
6. Return the artifact path and hash plus:
   `/higurashi-loop:deliver <ID>`.

Never directly write a requirement, configuration, or artifact from the
coordinator; the deterministic import command is the only permitted bootstrap
mutation. Never persist raw dialogue, plan, implement, commit, push, or invoke
the delivery agents.
